{"text": "Phone Number\nEmail\nAddress\nlinkedin.com/in/eve\n\nAreas of Expertise\n\nFundraising + Strategic Communication\nProject Management\nWriting/Editing + Digital Marketing \u00bb Analytics\nInterpersonal Relations * Brand Management\nTeam Leadership * Process Innovation\n\nPersonal Objective\n\nExperienced Communications Manager and\ndata lover seeking a Strategic Communications\nand Fundraising Role. | hope to use my strong\npeople and project management skills to\nenhance efficiency and deliver effective\nstrategies and creative solutions.\n\nEducation\n\nUNIVERSITY NAME\n\nTeacher's Education Program\n2008 - 2009\n\nUNIVERSITY NAME\n\nB.A. (Hons) English and History\n2002 - 2005\n\nSkills and Credentials\n\nStrategic fundraising professional with eight years of communications\nexperience: insights-driven content creation, editing, and strategic planning for\nboth digital and print fundraising campaigns.\nDemonstrated ability to manage a high capacity, cross-functional workload\naccurately and efficiently.\nConfident team leader who is adept at building relationships with all levels of\ninternal and external stakeholders.\n\nExperience\n\nCOMMUNICATIONS MANAGER | A CHARITY\nJan 2020 - Present\nDeveloping and leading the strategic communications plan to achieve a 45% growth in\nrevenue.\nManaging a small but mighty team to maximize the annual communications budget for a\nrecreation non-profit.\nAnalyzing digital marketing metrics & donor trends to draw insights from data to lead\ncommunications, branding, PR and fundraising initiatives and cross-functional projects -\nincl. an innovative organizational data tracking project to visualize org impact.\nCreating a wide range of materials for internal and external stakeholders including\nfunding proposals, reports, press releases, emails, articles, and digital content.\nIncreased average page views per month by 150% & online donations by 50% in 2020\nLeading team of content creators including website, print, SEO/SEM, email, and social\nmedia.\n\nDEVELOPMENT & COMMUNICATIONS OFFICER | A CHARITY\nOct 2014 \u2014 Dec 2019\nSuccessfully writing grant proposals and visualizing impact data for reporting,\nensuring recurring funding and revenue growth.\nOrganizing fundraising events including galas generating $100k revenue year on year.\nDevising, writing, and creating content (images/articles/brochures/email/video) for\nuse of both internal and external stakeholders.\nManaging contract staff, consultants, and volunteers.\nUsing a data-based approach to inform Google Ads, SEO and Content strategy,\nincreasing new donors each year against an industry trend of diminishing donor pool.\n\nMARKETING ASSISTANT AND CONTENT CREATOR | CONSULTANCY\nOct 20138 - Dec 2018\n\nMarketing duties: marketing research - Canadian B2B events; copywriting and\nediting; database administration; segmentation and marketing branding.\n\nACCOUNT RELATIONS COORDINATOR | INTERNATIONAL FOOD\nCOMPANY\nNov 2012 - Sept 2014\n\nFacilitating negotiations between internal colleagues and external customers.\nUsing interpersonal skills to build positive relationships and find creative solutions\nto resolve disputes to recoup thousands of dollars.\n\nTEACHER OF ENGLISH | A HIGH SCHOOL\nJul 2009 - Jul 2012\n\nHigh School English Teacher\nPromotion to second in charge of year group where | managed a team of 7 staff.\nCollaborative research, planning and evaluation for whole-school improvement.",
